[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Electrical wiring and sheet persistence

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-WIRING-LABEL-001
TITLE: Named terminal connections
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor shall assign or clear one label per terminal. Matching names shall connect the labeled terminals for circuit checks and simulation using ordinal case-insensitive comparison. The editor shall display the assigned spelling and refuse invalid labels before changing the sheet.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SetNetLabel, Board.Neighbors and WiringDocumentTests. The browser and MCP smoke tests replace a physical RC probe wire with matching labels and solve the reloaded circuit.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-WIRING-ROUTE-001
TITLE: Separate route geometry from topology
STATEMENT: >>>
The editor shall replace the ordered bends of an existing wire without changing its endpoints or electrically connecting nearby wires. An explicit junction shall join two distinct wires at a bend recorded on both routes. Removing that junction shall preserve the routes. Editing a joined route shall preserve its junction anchors. Deleting a wire shall remove its route and incident junctions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SetWireRoute, JoinRoutes, DeleteJunction, DeleteWire and Board.Neighbors. Verify a geometric crossing, an explicit join, join removal, undo and round trip.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-SHEET-JSON-001
TITLE: Validate and restore a versioned circuit sheet
STATEMENT: >>>
Saving shall export schema version 1, the parts and their values and geometry, terminal wires, labels, bends, junctions and part identifier counters without changing the revision. Loading shall validate the entire document before replacing the board, reject unsupported versions, invalid references and stale revisions, and record a successful replacement as one undoable edit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SaveDocument, LoadDocument and Board.Load. The browser stores one sheet per origin. MCP returns or accepts the same JSON for client-managed storage. Browser view state, undo history and analysis runs are outside this schema.
<<<
